+# Bulk link creation
+
+Create up to 100 short links in one request. Each item is processed independently and reported in
+request order, so one invalid URL never prevents the others from being created.
+
+## Endpoint
+
+`POST /api/v1/links/bulk` - satisfies **FR-1**
+
+```json
+{ "items": [ { "url": "https://example.com/a" }, { "url": "javascript:alert(1)" } ] }
+```
+
+Response `200 OK`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "created": 1,
+  "failed": 1,
+  "results": [
+    { "index": 0, "status": "created", "link": { "code": "aB3xY9z", "shortUrl": "http://localhost:8080/aB3xY9z" } },
+    { "index": 1, "status": "error", "error": { "status": 400, "detail": "Only http and https URLs are supported" } }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Semantics
+
+- **FR-2** Partial success: each item runs in its own transaction through the same `LinkService.create`
+  used by `POST /api/v1/links`. Item errors carry the HTTP status the single-create API would have returned
+  (`400` invalid URL/alias, `409` alias conflict).
+- **FR-3** Batch-shape errors (`items` missing, empty, or more than 100 entries) fail the whole request with
+  `400` and an RFC 9457 problem detail; nothing is created.
+
+## Limitations
+
+- `Idempotency-Key` is not supported for bulk requests yet; retrying a partially failed batch can create
+  duplicates for items that already succeeded. Retry only the failed indexes.
+- A bulk request consumes a single rate-limit token (bounded by the 100-item cap).
